  "question": {
    "text": "On complete combustion, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>492</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of an organic compound gave <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>792</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>%</mo></math> of carbon in the organic compound is (Nearest integer)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "44",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>44</mn></math>&nbsp;grams of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;contain&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn></math>&nbsp;grams of carbon.</p><p>Hence, one gram of&nbsp;carbon dioxide contain&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>12</mn><mn>44</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;gram of carbon.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>792</mn></math>&nbsp;gram of carbon dioxide contain&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>12</mn><mn>44</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>792</mn></math>&nbsp;gram of carbon</p><p>Percentage of carbon =&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mtext>Mass&#160;of&#160;carbon</mtext><mtext>Mass&#160;of&#160;organic&#160;compound</mtext></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>100</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mn>12</mn><mn>44</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>792</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>492</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>43</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>%</mo></math></p><p>So, answer is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>44</mn></math>.</p>",
